      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T06:08:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed. The probe and the errcb observe the same underlying watch-error state. PS3 handles error callbacks throughout initial registration, including before the cookie is published, so the periodic probe is no longer necessary and has been removed. Recovery is initiated by the errcb, with backoff for failed re-registration.\n\nOne separate caveat, reproduced on vstart: a stalled watcher whose session is reset can miss a notification if the notification times out but the watch registration survives until reconnect. The OSD removes the expired notification from the pending list, then successfully reconnects the existing watch without an errcb. That notification is not replayed.\n\nFor RADOS_URLS, the export change is then missed until another reload. Keeping the old probe would not address this either, since the watch remains valid. A periodic reload would provide a fallback, which I\u0027d propose separately.",
